Conversion to Boolean
   
     In boolean converting any number into boolean type is always true except 0.
      both positive and negative numbers are true, 0 alone false;
      1 ----> true 
      0 ----> false
      Example :
              let x = 23;  or let x = -27;  same output true 
              x = Boolean(x);
              console.log(x); ---->output:true

                 let x = 0;  
              x = Boolean(x);
              console.log(x); ---->output:false
        in js if we pass any string it is always true even space also. if the string is empty it shows false.

        EG :
            let x = "apple";
            x = Boolean(x);
            console.log(typeof x); ----->output : true

            let x = "";
            x = Boolean(x);
            console.log(typeof x); ----->output : false

            let x = " "; ----> even it consider space.
            x = Boolean(x);
            console.log(typeof x); ----->output : true








